    "narrative": "The cornerstone of today\u2019s offensive attack is **Corbin Carroll**, who leads the roster with an elite 80.64 score. Facing Bradley, **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a high-upside matchup where a slow-delivering pitcher creates a prime environment for his elite stolen base potential. Joining him in the \"Strong\" tier is **Tyler Soderstrom** (76.91) and **Seiya Suzuki** (71.48); **Tyler Soderstrom** draws a favorable park-adjusted matchup against Ure\u00f1a, while **Seiya Suzuki** finds himself in a high-leverage spot hitting third against the struggling Corbin, capitalizing on a significant skill-gap advantage. Furthermore, **Jose Caballero** (75.83) serves as an essential engine for our speed-first strategy today; his dynamic platoon edge against Abbott, coupled with a wind-aided environment, makes him a lock for our UTIL spot.\n\nThe most difficult benching decision involved **Brice Turang**, who finished with a 45.62 efficiency score. While **Brice Turang** provides consistent value, he was squeezed out of the starting nine by the superior situational projections of **Alex Freeland** and **Max Muncy**. Though **Max Muncy** carries an \"Elite Catcher\" risk factor today, his high raw scoring potential against Ure\u00f1a made him impossible to bench. We remain cautious with several \"Lineup Pending\" designations\u2014specifically for **Gabriel Moreno**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Josh Naylor**, **Max Muncy**, **Alex Freeland**, **Corbin Carroll**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, and **Henry Bolte**. Should those official lineups deviate significantly from our assumptions, particularly regarding batting order protection for **Gabriel Moreno** and **Josh Naylor**, we may see downward volatility in their final production. **Vinnie Pasquantino** remains sidelined on the IL, leaving our infield depth to be managed by the remaining core.",
